# Copy this file to `harness/.env.harness.local` and fill in the keys for the
# labs you actually want to watch:
#
#   cp harness/.env.harness.example harness/.env.harness.local
#
# Then use `--env-file=harness/.env.harness.local` everywhere the docs show
# it. `node harness/cli/init.mjs` writes this copy for you on import, and
# never overwrites one that already exists, not even with --force.
#
# WHY NOT `.env`: never name it that, and never merge it into one. Most real
# projects already keep a `.env` at the root for the application itself —
# a database URL, a deploy token, a publishable key — and an earlier version
# of this file told you to copy over it, which destroys that file outright.
# The two are separate on purpose: your web server has no reason to hold nine
# labs' API keys, and this harness has no reason to hold your database's
# service-role key. `.env.harness` / `.env.harness.local` cannot collide with
# a project `.env` no matter what the project already does.
#
# WHERE: inside `harness/`, beside the code that reads it. That keeps the
# harness self-contained and the project root clean. The one cost: an
# upgrade replaces this whole directory, so PRESERVE `.env.harness.local`
# across a re-import — copy it aside first, or re-import everything except
# that file. Losing it costs you the keys, nothing else.
#
# COMMITTED vs LOCAL: `.env.harness.example` (this file, placeholders only)
# is the one that belongs in git. `.env.harness.local` holds the real keys
# and must never be committed. Filling the keys into this file instead is
# the mistake the two names exist to prevent — this one is tracked.
#
# Make sure .gitignore covers it. A `.env.*` line with no leading slash does,
# at every level including `harness/`; a bare `.env` line does NOT, and
# several real projects list `.env.local`, `.env.production.local` and friends
# individually, which misses `.env.harness.local` entirely. Check with
# `git check-ignore -v harness/.env.harness.local` rather than assuming.
#
# Read locally via `node --env-file=<file> ...`. It has nothing to do with
# GitHub Actions, which reads secrets from the repo's own Settings -> Secrets
# instead. See the "Getting started" section of the root README.md.
#
# You do NOT need every key below. Only add a key for a lab you want the
# detector to watch — an unwatched lab costs nothing, and a watched lab with
# no key is reported "skipped", never a silent failure.

# --- Provider API keys (all optional; add only what you're watching) ------
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
QWEN_API_KEY=
XAI_API_KEY=
META_API_KEY=
ZAI_API_KEY=

# --- Detector configuration (optional; all have sane defaults) ------------

# Comma-separated list of provider names to check. Defaults to every
# provider that's been imported (harness/providers/index.mjs imports all 9).
# PROVIDERS_WATCHED=anthropic,openai,google

# Where the "which models have I already seen" state lives. Defaults to
# .agent/model-snapshot.json under wherever you run the script from.
# MODEL_SNAPSHOT_PATH=.agent/model-snapshot.json

# Ceiling on how many newly-released models one run may fan out to. Not a
# cost control — it's a blast-radius limit for the pathological case where a
# catalogue rename makes many ids look new on the same run.
# MAX_FANOUT=8

# --- Local stand-in for every lab (testing only) ---------------------------

# Send every lab request — model calls and catalogue listings alike — to a
# loopback server instead of the labs, keeping each provider's real path,
# headers and body. Honoured ONLY for localhost / 127.0.0.1 / ::1; anything
# else is refused before a byte is sent, because the request carries the
# key. This is how tests/e2e/mock-labs.test.mjs drives the whole chain with
# no key and no bill (tests/helpers/mock-labs.mjs is the stand-in). Never
# set it for a real run.
# HARNESS_LAB_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4010

# --- Reachability probe (optional) -----------------------------------------

# A pre-call estimate of your real prompt's size in tokens, used only to
# skip a candidate whose provider-reported context window plainly can't fit
# it. Most providers don't report a window at all, so this rarely matters
# yet. There's no estimator wired up in this harness today (see
# Portable-Harness-Design.md — the context compiler isn't ported), so leave
# this unset until you have a real number to give it.
# CONTEXT_ESTIMATE_TOKENS=

# --- Notifications (LIVE) ---------------------------------------------------
#
# The digest — a plain-language email about what each cycle did, with a
# reliable terse fallback if the model call writing it fails. Read by
# harness/scripts/send-digest.mjs and send-escalation-notice.mjs via
# harness/lib/notify.mjs, and sent automatically by the generated workflow.
#
# The variable name follows the sender you configure: notify.provider in
# project-adapter.yml names a sender registered through notify.mjs's
# registerSender(), and its key is read from <PROVIDER>_API_KEY. SendGrid
# ships built in; a Slack, webhook or other email sender is added by
# registering one under its own name, with no change to harness code.
SENDGRID_API_KEY=

# --- Not built — do not add real values for these ---------------------------
#
# The reference implementation also collects player feedback through Supabase
# and folds it into the suggestion prompt. That has NOT been ported: nothing
# here reads SUPABASE_URL or SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, so setting them does nothing.
# The context-pack section they would feed is simply omitted when absent —
# see harness/lib/context-pack.mjs and principle 18, never claim data you did
# not supply.
